  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Knowledge that carries into later work",
      "items": [
        "Preserve originals, curate meaning, make justified connections, reuse for a new question, revise as a new version.",
        "Continue from stored originals and notes rather than a prior conversation. Explicitly supply the kit and profile to a fresh session."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Files are the durable record",
      "items": [
        "sources/<id>/content.raw + provenance.json: original bytes and provenance",
        "concepts/<id>/rNNNNNN.md: body, evidence, links and previous revision",
        "index.md: CLI-managed current links plus a separate human navigation area maintained by an authorized agent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Separate agent and CLI roles",
      "items": [
        "The agent reads authorized material and prepares Markdown outside the bundle. The CLI validates and stores prepared writing.",
        "capture / curate / annotate / review; recall / search / show / history / diff",
        "context / graph / health / eval-retrieval; check / inspect-storage",
        "The dashed path bypasses the CLI for direct reading. A profile is agent-interpreted data, not CLI-enforced permissions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Current implementation boundaries",
      "items": [
        "The CLI calls no model or network. External agent model use and text transfer require separate authorization.",
        "Locks, request IDs and current-revision comparisons protect writes, without full transactions or automatic recovery.",
        "Relations and freshness diagnostics reflect recorded declarations. They do not replace semantic judgment or fact verification.",
        "The showcase and videos explain the product. A note-editing GUI, MCP server and vector database are not part of the current system."
      ]
    }
  ]
